2026-11-02  Krishap  <krishapbusiness@gmail.com>

	Do not rebuild in make check and make install.

	* Makefile.in (BINARIES, CARGO_ENV): New.
	(all): Depend on the binaries instead of the phony build target.
	Make them real targets, using the dependency files cargo writes,
	so that make install does not run cargo again.
	(check): Depend on the binaries; pass the cargo environment and
	flags to the test script.
	* tests/run-tests.sh: Build the tests in the release profile,
	reusing the dependencies make built.
	* INSTALL: Advise running make before sudo make install.

2026-11-02  Krishap  <krishapbusiness@gmail.com>

	Install the programs set-group-ID gkey, so that programs running
	as the user cannot use the TPM.

	* src/privilege.rs: New file.  Detect set-group-ID runs, remove
	unsafe environment variables, drop the group, warn about group
	memberships that defeat the protection.
	* src/bin/gkey-service/main.rs (main): Refuse --tcti, --uhid and
	--verify=command when set-group-ID; always use /dev/tpmrm0.
	(serve): Drop the group once the TPM and UHID device are open.
	* src/bin/gkey/main.rs (main, run): Likewise, after opening the TPM.
	* src/ctap2.rs (spawn): Do not open the keystore at startup.
	* data/70-gkey.rules: Rename to...
	* data/70-gkey.rules.in: ...this.  Grant the gkey group the TPM
	through an ACL.
	* data/gkey.sysusers.in: New file.
	* data/gkey.service.in: Warn against NoNewPrivileges.
	* configure.ac: Look for setfacl.  New options --with-gkey-group
	and --with-sysusersdir.
	* Makefile.in (install-setgid): New target.
	* doc/gkey.texi, README.md, INSTALL, DESIGN.md, NEWS: Update.

2026-11-02  Krishap  <krishapbusiness@gmail.com>

	Ask polkit for consent instead of pinentry and PAM.

	* src/polkit.rs: New file.  polkit client checking authorizations
	for the service's own process.
	* src/verify.rs (Operation): New.
	(Method::Polkit): New, the default.
	(Method::Pam): Remove, with the PAM and pinentry code.
	* src/ctap2.rs (Authenticator::consent): Pass the operation.
	* src/bin/gkey-service/main.rs: Use a multi-threaded runtime.
	Remove the --pam-service and --pinentry options.
	* data/io.github.krishap_s.gkey.policy: New file.
	* data/gkey.pam: Remove.
	* configure.ac, Makefile.in: Install the polkit actions; drop PAM.
	* Cargo.toml: Depend on zbus.
	* default.nix: Drop linux-pam.
	* doc/gkey.texi, README.md, INSTALL, DESIGN.md, NEWS: Update.

2026-10-28  Krishap  <krishapbusiness@gmail.com>

	Support Rust 1.80, so that Cargo versions without edition 2024
	support can build gkey.

	* Cargo.toml (rust-version): Set to 1.80.
	* Cargo.lock: Resolve dependency versions compatible with it,
	notably tss-esapi 7.6 and zeroize 1.8.
	* src/uhid.rs (UHIDDevice::create): Allow the deprecation of
	AsyncFd::new.
	* INSTALL: Update the Rust requirement.

2026-10-28  Krishap  <krishapbusiness@gmail.com>

	Implement a TPM backed FIDO2 authenticator.

	* src/tpm.rs: New file.  Storage primary key, signing keys,
	sealing, salted parameter encrypted session.
	* src/keystore.rs: New file.  Credential list encrypted with a
	TPM sealed AES-256-GCM key.
	* src/ctaphid.rs: New file.  CTAPHID transport.
	* src/ctap2.rs: New file.  CTAP 2.0 authenticator.
	* src/verify.rs: New file.  User presence and verification with
	pinentry, PAM, or an external command.
	* src/getopt.rs: New file.  GNU style option parsing.
	* src/uhid.rs: Rewrite without generated bindings.
	* src/bin/gkey-service/main.rs: Serve the authenticator.
	* src/bin/gkey/main.rs: New program to manage credentials.
	* src/ctap2/, src/infra/, src/utils/: Remove.
	* tests/authenticator.rs, tests/fido2-client.py:
	* tests/run-tests.sh, examples/socket-authenticator.rs: New files.
	* doc/gkey.texi: New manual.
	* data/: systemd user unit, udev rule, PAM configuration and
	kernel module list.
	* configure.ac, Makefile.in: Check for tpm2-tss and PAM; provide
	the standard GNU targets.
	* LICENSE: Rename to COPYING.
	* AUTHORS, INSTALL, NEWS, ChangeLog: New files.
	* Cargo.toml: Replace uhid-virt and passkey-transports with
	tss-esapi, ciborium and aes-gcm.
	* default.nix, flake.nix: Build with tpm2-tss and PAM.
